1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,840
Moving on to number four buy the best gear that you can afford.
接下来是第四点：作者建议，在自己负担得起的范围内买好装备。

2
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:10,270
Um I remember my mate ben telling me that buy cheap buy twice.
我记得朋友本告诉我：“买便宜货，往往要买两次。”

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:18,720
And a lot of the time that really is the case I find it's been the same with any hobby I've done you tend to buy the cheapest entry level gear.
很多时候，我发现确实如此。我做过的爱好也一样，人往往先买最便宜的入门装备。

4
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:22,239
And before long you're wanting to upgrade all the time.
没过多久，你就一直想升级了。

5
00:00:22,239 --> 00:00:30,190
So if you start off buying something that is decent quality and affordable it's going to last you longer.
所以在他看来，如果一开始就买质量不错、价格负担得起的东西，它能用得更久。

6
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:36,320
And if you're not sure if you're going to like it or not it's a really good idea to either either borrow some gear or buy secondhand gear.
如果还不确定自己会不会喜欢，他觉得借些装备或买二手的会是好主意。

7
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:40,160
That way I feel like that you're not really risking any money at all.
这样一来，我觉得就没怎么冒损失钱的风险。

8
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:48,480
Secondhand gear tends to hold its price really well so if you were to buy a biv like this and you paid 150 for it secondhand.
二手装备往往比较保值。他举例说，像这样的露营袋，二手买来花了150。

9
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:56,559
If you didn't like it you could sell it the following week or the following month and mo in most cases get your 150 back.
如果不喜欢，下周或下个月再卖掉，多数情况下能收回那150。

10
00:00:56,559 --> 00:01:03,880
Make sure to do plenty of research and try and buy gear that's going to be suitable for the type of camping that you're going to be doing.
作者还建议充分研究，购买适合自己将进行的露营类型的装备。

11
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:15,870
So if you're only going to be camping in the summer months you do not need to spend 000 on a four season hillberg all singing all danc in tent.
比如，如果只在夏天露营，他说就不用花一大笔钱买某款功能齐全的四季帐篷。

12
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:21,239
You can get something for a fraction of that price that will do the job that you need perfectly well.
他认为，用那价格的一小部分，也能买到完全满足自己需要的东西。

13
00:01:21,239 --> 00:01:28,040
And one thing to remember expensive gear doesn't always mean good gear and cheap gear doesn't always mean bad gear.
还要记住：贵的装备不一定好，便宜的也不一定差。

14
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:39,750
Number five don't believe the hype there's a lot of people out there including self that get sucked into all of this fancy marketing that the the gear companies put out there.
第五点：别盲信炒作。包括他自己在内，很多人都会被装备公司的花哨营销吸引进去。

15
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:49,080
Maybe you've just bought the latest plastic water bottle and then two weeks later there's another fancier plastic water bottle comes out.
也许你刚买了最新款塑料水瓶，两周后又出了一款更花哨的。

16
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,960
With a bit thicker plastic but it does exactly the same job.
塑料稍厚一点，但干的活完全一样。

17
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:57,799
I get frustrated by companies that make incremental upgrades.
那些一点一点升级产品的公司会让我感到烦躁。

18
00:01:57,799 --> 00:02:03,999
They they might have ideas in their head that could make the perfect tent or the perfect action camera now.
他们也许现在就有想法，能做出完美的帐篷或运动相机。

19
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:12,200
But they don't want to give you the perfect action camera this year what they want to do is give you a little bit each year.
但他觉得，公司不想今年就给你完美的相机，而是每年只给一点点改进。

20
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:17,440
So you keep coming back and keep coming back and buying the next best thing.
这样你就会不停回头买，追逐下一件更好的产品。

21
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:21,080
I know it's not camping related but things like the iphone.
我知道这不算露营话题，不过像手机就是这样。

22
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:26,760
Um I used to upgrade my phone pretty much every year but I skipped the iphone 15.
以前我几乎每年都换手机，但我跳过了iPhone 15。

23
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:32,360
Instead of upgrading your kit every year upgrade every few years and then maybe you notice a difference in performance.
作者觉得，与其每年换装备，不如隔几年换一次，那样也许才更能察觉性能差别。

24
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:43,520
And also getting sucked in by the hypee can lead to impulse buying where you're buying stuff that you don't really need it doesn't add to the experience.
此外，被炒作吸引会导致冲动消费，买来并不真正需要、也不能增进体验的东西。

25
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:50,600
And before you know it you need an 80 l backpack to to put all the crap in that you've accumulated.
不知不觉，你就需要一个80升的背包，来装那些越积越多的杂物。

26
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:54,359
Number six organize your gear effectively.
第六点：有效地整理你的装备。

27
00:02:54,359 --> 00:02:59,040
Um I'm not the best person when it comes to actually store in my gear.
嗯，说到收纳装备，我可不是最擅长的人。

28
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:02,480
I can't always put my hands on the thing that I really want.
我不总能马上找到自己真正想用的东西。

29
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:13,720
If you've got organized one it will highlight if you've got too much of something maybe if you got all your stoves in one location you might find that you've got 30 of them.
如果整理好了，一来能看出某样东西是否太多。比如把炉具都放一处，你可能发现自己有30个。

30
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:18,600
More importantly organizing the kit that you put in your backpack now there's lots of videos out there.
更重要的是整理放进背包里的装备。网上有很多相关视频。

31
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:26,480
That show you how to pack your backpack um but that's not necessarily the right way for you.
这些视频教你怎么装背包，但那不一定就是适合你的方式。

32
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:29,880
Make sure you've got easy access to the things that you need.
他主张让需要的物品容易拿到。

33
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:39,320
So if you've got a medical condition for example there's no point in having your first aid kit with your medication right at the bottom of your backpack.
作者举例，如果有健康状况要处理，把装着药的急救包塞在背包最底下，就不方便了。

34
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:47,840
Think about the weather if it's going to be raining you want your shelter close to the top of your pack or somewhere maybe on the outside of your pack where it's easy to get to.
他还说要考虑天气。若会下雨，就把遮蔽物放靠近包顶的位置，或包外等容易拿到的地方。

35
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:53,679
You want to be able to put your shelter up first so you can unpack your backpack in a dry environment.
作者想先把遮蔽物搭好，再在干燥的环境中打开背包。

36
00:03:53,679 --> 00:04:00,720
Water to stay hydrated snacks to keep your energy up just make sure you've got system so you know where things are when you need them.
水用来补充水分，零食用来补充能量。他最后强调有一套收纳方法，确保需要时知道物品在哪。
